{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_adr_0199_a_set_is_a_playlist_mixed_by_one_engine_decision", "label": "ADR 0199: A set is a playlist laid out on one beat clock, mixed by one engine for the preview and the file", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/adr/0199-a-set-is-a-playlist-mixed-by-one-engine.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user asked for a set builder (a playlist turned into a mix, transitions controlled, 2 or 3 decks, automix styles), then said the export is the end product. Chosen: WAV 24-bit and MP3 320, GLUE plans every transition and the user moves points, rendering in the browser with one engine for listening and for the file, key lock on. Playback had one HTMLAudioElement and no mixing. Rejected: Web Audio nodes (no key lock, an OfflineAudioContext holds the whole set in memory, live and offline not sample-identical); rendering in GLUE Home in Rust (a second engine that must sound identical); time-stretch libraries (Rubber Band is GPL, SoundTouch LGPL in a web bundle; Signalsmith MIT kept as the fallback); positions accumulated sample by sample (they drift). WSOLA chosen: small, deterministic, testable, and DJ tempo changes are small (plus or minus 8 %)."}], "edges": [{"source": "vault_adr_0199_a_set_is_a_playlist_mixed_by_one_engine_decision", "target": "src_core_sets_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0199-a-set-is-a-playlist-mixed-by-one-engine.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0199_a_set_is_a_playlist_mixed_by_one_engine_decision", "target": "src_core_sets_tempo", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/adr/0199-a-set-is-a-playlist-mixed-by-one-engine.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_adr_0199_a_set_is_a_playlist_mixed_by_one_engine_decision", "target": "src